<title>USA: Hi-Tech Pharmacal generic drug approved.</title>
<headline>Hi-Tech Pharmacal generic drug approved.</headline>
<dateline>AMITYVILLE, N.Y. 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hi-Tech Pharmacal Co Inc said on Wednesday that it has received U.S. Food and Drug Administration approval for the company to market a generic erythromycin topical solution that is equivalent to T-Stat Solution two percent.</p>
<p>Hi-Tech's Erythro-Statin 2 percent will be marketed to treat acne, the company said. Bristol-Myers Squibb Co makes T-Stat Solution, Hi-Tech said.</p>
<p>The company said this approval is its first for a dermatological product and it expects to focus some of its efforts in the future in this field.</p>
</text>
